  "source_checks": [
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "Let p be prime, 3<=c<p odd, r>=2, s>r, N=p^r, and q any characteristic-zero primitive p^s-th root.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 7,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "scope_and_degree"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "e=v(p)=(p-1)p^(s-1), B=r(p-1)p^(r-1)/2,\n    K=cN/2+cB, E=(c-1)N/2+cB, D=N+E-p,",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 15,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "B_and_K"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "h=floor(r/2), beta=p^h, L=N/beta,",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 17,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "h_beta_L"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "- Every noncentral disk contains cL roots, comprising (c-1)L boundary roots and L strict-interior roots. All these roots have v(X)=p^ord_p(a).\n- The central disk contains cL+1 roots, comprising (c-1)L boundary roots and L+1 strict-interior roots. None is zero.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 36,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "all_disk_counts"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "The disjoint counts sum to (beta-1)cL+(cL+1)=cN+1, so the root cover is complete and no shallow roots are missing.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 148,
      "source_section": "Section 4",
      "summary_item": "disjoint_total"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "There is no zero root, and v(F(0))=N+E.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 30,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "no_zero_root"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "- For r=2, all p+1 central strict-interior roots have exactly v(X)=p^2/(p+1). For r>=3, no individual deeper interior depth is asserted.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 38,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "r2_central_interior_depth"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "For r>=3 there are no exceptions. For r=2 put d=p(p-1)/2 and choose mu^2=t^p. In the central coordinate X=mu Y, U=Y^2, the exceptional class exists precisely when p divides b_c. It consists of exactly 2p roots, counted with multiplicity, with residual U=-1.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 44,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "exception_scope_and_count"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "v(U+1)>1,\n    v(F'(xi))=K+d+1.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 46,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "exception_depth_and_derivative"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "b_c=R_c(-1), so M_c(Z)=Z R_c(Z^2).",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 26,
      "source_section": "Section 1",
      "summary_item": "b_c_definition"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "J=XF'-F=X^2 A'+aM-aXM'.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 164,
      "source_section": "Sections 5 and 7",
      "summary_item": "odd_operator"
    },
    {
      "checked": "MATCHES_ACCEPTED_PROOF",
      "exact_source_excerpt": "J=t^S(2U f_U-f),\n    weight(2U f_U-f)>=d.",
      "source": "author/REPORT.md",
      "source_line_start": 302,
      "source_section": "Section 7",
